<title>USA: Reeds &quot;cautiously optimistic&quot; for year.</title>
<headline>Reeds &quot;cautiously optimistic&quot; for year.</headline>
<dateline>WILMINGTON, N.C. 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Reeds Jewelers Inc said Wednesday it was &quot;cautiously optimistic&quot; that it will meet its sales and earnings goals for the rest of the fiscal year.</p>
<p>Reeds did not disclose its financial goals.</p>
<p>In the third quarter, ended November 30, Reeds earned $239,000, or $0.06 a share, on net sales of $21.8 million, compared to earnings of $219,000, or $0.05 a share, on sales of $21.2 million a year earlier.</p>
<p>For the full year, analysts expect Reeds to earn $1.00 a share, up from $0.82 last year, according to First Call.</p>
